1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,640
If you shattered your wrist,

2
00:00:01,680 --> 00:00:04,040
imagine gluing the bones back together.

3
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:05,960
Researchers actually did it.

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,760
They developed an experimental glue

5
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:10,280
inspired by oysters sticking to rocks.

6
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:11,960
It grips bone even inside

7
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,640
a wet, bloody wound.

8
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:15,320
In one reported wrist case,

9
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:17,000
surgeons secured the broken pieces

10
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:18,760
in just three minutes.

11
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:21,080
The fracture still needed months to heal.

12
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:22,627
But as new bone grows,

13
00:00:22,667 --> 00:00:24,760
the glue gradually disappears.

14
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:25,960
Your body replaces

15
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,740
the stuff holding you together.

